      "source": [
        "# 1.2 Retrieving text from movies\n",
        "## 1.2.1  Get content of an article: a comparison of content extraction methods"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Yet, we only have the movie titles that we will use for our project. To construct a complete corpus that can be studied with an NLP Pipeline, we need to retrieve the text of the wikipedia's page associated with the movie title, along with the page categories.\n",
        "\n",
        "To do so, we need to define another GET method that will allow us to \"scrape\" all the content from a specific page, given the movie's title.\n",
        "Using the code template given for this project, we complete the two proposed methods that achieve this objective. The first one is using the 'revisions' module, while the second uses the 'extracts' module. After coding and commenting these methods, we give a detailed explanation for each of them, and conclude by highlighting the main difference.\n",
        "\n",
        "We noticed that the Wikipedia's API returns a nested JSON hierarchy (with the path query -> pages -> page ID -> property). This structure allows Wikipedia to store multiple properties (*e.g.* revisions and categories) within a single object, which reflects the \"relational\" nature of the metadata, and motivates the use of a recursive parsing approach."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jhnoAF9AeFex"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "lvlMKyB8vPWt",
        "collapsed": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def get_page_content_all(title):\n",
        "  \"\"\" Request the content of a chosen page from the English Wikipedia API, using the 'revisions' module.\n",
        "  \"\"\"\n",
        "  base_url = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php\" # The API endpoint\n",
        "\n",
        "  params = {\n",
        "        'action': 'query',\n",
        "        'prop': 'revisions|categories',\n",
        "        'titles': title,\n",
        "        'rvprop': 'content', # Retrieve the content of each pages associated to each movie title\n",
        "        'cllimit': 'max',  # We want to retrieve all the categories\n",
        "        'format': 'json'\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "  try:\n",
        "      response = requests.get(base_url, headers=headers, params=params) # We make the API request\n",
        "      response.raise_for_status()\n",
        "      data = response.json()\n",
        "\n",
        "      # The API will return an ID associated to the specific movie's page, and we use it\n",
        "      # to retrieve the content's page\n",
        "      pages = data.get('query', {}).get('pages', {})\n",
        "      page_id = list(pages.keys())[0] # We use the ID of the page to access the data:\n",
        "                                        # because the page's ID change each time,\n",
        "      page_data = pages[page_id]      # we must navigate dynamically throught the JSON\n",
        "\n",
        "      # The JSON path is as follows: pages -> page_id -> revisions -> list -> index 0 -> '*' (all),\n",
        "      #where '*' contains the Wikitext\n",
        "      revisions = page_data.get('revisions', [])\n",
        "      if revisions:\n",
        "          content = revisions[0].get('*', \"\") # The raw content is within the key '*'\n",
        "\n",
        "      else:\n",
        "          content = \"\"\n",
        "      # Then, we extract the associated categories:\n",
        "      # This time, the JSON path is: pages -> page_id -> categories\n",
        "      categories_raw = page_data.get('categories', [])\n",
        "      categories = [cat['title'] for cat in categories_raw] # We want to keep only the\n",
        "                                                              # title of the categories\n",
        "      return content, categories\n",
        "\n",
        "  except Exception as e:\n",
        "      print(f\"Error occured while retrieving the text for''{title}': {e}\")\n",
        "      return \"\", []"
      ]
    },
