      "source": [
        "## 1.2.2 Get labels by proxy\n",
        "\n",
        "We seek the genre of the movies that we extracted from the Wikipedia API. However, the Wikipedia API does not have a specific unique and clean category \"genre\", which motivates the use for *proxy-labeling*: we will use the categories, which are just content generated by users, as an approximation (or proxy) to infer the genre of the movie.\n",
        "This involves retrieving all Wikipedia categories associated with an article, and filtering them against a curated list of genre-related keywords. To do so, we first need to define a list of keywords that we will use for the genres. It is given by the templates and re-used hereafter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rrudxvA1g9UG"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# We use a pre-defined list of genres (keywords) within which we will seek for the genre of our movies\n",
        "\n",
        "genre_keywords = [\n",
        "    'action', 'adventure', 'animation', 'biographical', 'comedy', 'crime', 'disaster',\n",
        "    'documentary', 'drama', 'epic', 'erotic', 'experimental', 'fantasy', 'film noir',\n",
        "    'historical', 'holiday', 'horror', 'independent', 'musical', 'mystery', 'noir',\n",
        "    'romance', 'romantic', 'satire', 'science fiction','silent', 'sports',\n",
        "    'spy', 'superhero', 'thriller', 'war', 'western'\n",
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We complete the `get_page_categories` method below. This method serves as the data collection layer, as it navigates into the hierarchical JSON structure of the API (going through the path query -> pages -> categories) in order to extract the full list of tags assigned to a movie by Wikipedia contributors (users)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f5RNlP1Zd8Iv"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ynvMsTzegtHF"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def get_page_categories(title):\n",
        "  \"\"\" Request the categories of a chosen page from the English Wikipedia API.\n",
        "  \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "  base_url = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php\"\n",
        "  params = {\n",
        "        'action': 'query',\n",
        "        'prop': 'categories',\n",
        "        'titles': title,\n",
        "        'cllimit': 'max',  # We retrieve the maximum of categories\n",
        "        'format': 'json'\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "  try:\n",
        "      response = requests.get(base_url, headers=headers, params=params) # We send the request to the API\n",
        "      response.raise_for_status()\n",
        "      data = response.json()\n",
        "\n",
        "      # We go throught the JSON file, following the path: query -> pages -> ID -> categories\n",
        "      pages = data.get('query', {}).get('pages', {})\n",
        "\n",
        "      if pages:\n",
        "          page_id = list(pages.keys())[0] # We retrieve the ID of the page\n",
        "          page_data = pages[page_id]\n",
        "\n",
        "          categories_raw = page_data.get('categories', []) # We extract the raw dictionnaries, and returns\n",
        "                                                             # an empty list if no categories is retrieved\n",
        "\n",
        "          categories = [cat['title'] for cat in categories_raw] # We clean the results by keeping only the\n",
        "      else:                                                     # title of each retrieved categorie\n",
        "          categories = []\n",
        "\n",
        "      return categories\n",
        "\n",
        "  except Exception as e:\n",
        "      print(f\"ErrError occured during the recuperation of categories for '{title}': {e}\")\n",
        "      return []"
      ]
    },
