        "As discussed during the course [1], processing raw  text is computationally challenging. We therefore need to transform it into discrete units of analysis through tokenization. For this project, we use the spaCy framework [2], specifically loading the `en_core_web_md` model. As explained during lab sessions [1], it is crucial to note that this object is not merely a tokenizer, but a full NLP pipeline containing a Part-of-Speech tagger, a dependency parser, and static word vectors. We chose the 'medium' (md) version specifically because it includes these vector representations, which offer better accuracy for syntactic analysis and similarity tasks."
      ],
