      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The previous cell shows us an overview of the wide-range of genre types that exists in our corpus. Furthemore, we need to recall that each movie can be associated with more than one genre, as the list format of the \"genres\" column shows. Even so this allows for a deeper understanding on the movie thema, it is harder for an unsupervised learning task than having a single label for each. However, this wide variety of genre does not mean that they are as \"unique\" as they seem. First, because some genres can be seen as close (think for example at \"romantic\" and \"drama\", or \"thriller\" and \"crime\"), and secondly because some genre can contain only a small quantity of movies among the 499, so some genres might be too rare in the \"genres column\". This is clearly shown by the barplot of the genres in section 2, where the 15th most occuring genre, \"fantasy\", appears already less than 20 times. We can easily imagine that genres between the 15th and the 28th are mentionned for a very few articles, maybe less than 5. Then, extrapolating this conjecture, if a genre appears only once, it would be difficult for the clustering procedure to identify clearly which movie belongs to this genre, as the procedure will only be guided by text features.\n",
