      "source": [
        "# Based on the previous analysis, we define the number of clusters for the spectral clustering\n",
        "n_clusters=8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The following method implement the spectral clustering. Note that we have performed a quick modification from the original template. Indeed, we  adapt the input for the NER-based matrix. According to the scikit-learn documentation for SpectralClustering [9], affinity='precomputed' states that the input must be an affinity matrix, *i.e.* where larger values of this matrix means greater similarity. However, as defined in section 5, our ner_distance is a Jaccard distance matrix, where 0 indicates perfect overlap while 1 indicates total dissimilarity. We thought that passing this matrix directly would invert the logic, causing the algorithm to cluster together the most dissimilar movies (treating distance 1 as high affinity). Therefore, in the function below, we explicitly convert the distance into an affinity using the transformation:\n",
        "$$\\text{affinity} = 1 - \\text{distance}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This ensures that pairs with a distance of 0 become an affinity of 1, correctly guiding the clustering process."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "EjRC-lHL0zg8"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "D2__73I_YGT-"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def spectral_cluster(distance_or_features, n_clusters=8, features=True):\n",
        "    \"\"\" Perform spectral clustering on the given distance or features.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    if features: # In the SBERT case, we have features vectors as inputs, so the function will\n",
        "        clustering = SpectralClustering( # calculate the affinity matrix by computing a graph of\n",
        "            n_clusters=n_clusters,       # nearest neighbors\n",
        "            affinity=\"nearest_neighbors\",\n",
        "            random_state=42\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        return clustering.fit_predict(distance_or_features)\n",
        "    else: # In the NER-based distance case, we have a Jaccard distance matrix, where a 0 value means that\n",
        "          # articles are close, and a value of 1 means that they are far away (no NER in common).\n",
        "          # We need to transform it into an \"affinity matrix\"\n",
        "        affinity_matrix = 1.0 - distance_or_features\n",
        "\n",
        "        clustering = SpectralClustering(\n",
        "            n_clusters=n_clusters,\n",
        "            affinity=\"precomputed\",\n",
        "            random_state=42\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        return clustering.fit_predict(affinity_matrix)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MVX4MJqeYO6K",
        "colab": {
